  "Question": "If the sequence \\(\\{a_n\\}\\) is defined by \\[ \\begin{aligned} a_1&=2,\\\\ a_{n+1}&=a_n+2n\\quad(n\\ge1), \\end{aligned} \\] then \\(a_{100}\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(9900\\)",
    "B": "\\(9902\\)",
    "C": "\\(9904\\)",
    "D": "\\(10100\\)",
    "E": "\\(10102\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "From \\(a_1\\) to \\(a_{100}\\), there are \\(99\\) steps. The recurrence says that the amounts added are \\(2,4,6,\\ldots,198\\).\n\nTo sum these equally spaced amounts, add the list to a reversed copy. Each of the \\(99\\) resulting pairs totals \\(200\\), so the original list totals \\(99\\cdot200/2\\). Therefore\n\\[\na_{100}=2+\\frac{99\\cdot200}{2}=9902.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{9902}\\), choice B.",
